{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01297",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.67,
      "end_seconds": 4.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Hi, sit anywhere you like. Alright, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.92,
      "end_seconds": 10.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got breathlessness on slopes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.39,
      "end_seconds": 13.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.34,
      "end_seconds": 18.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.03,
      "end_seconds": 23.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "So, has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.01,
      "end_seconds": 28.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "For about a year, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.49,
      "end_seconds": 38.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "Okay, can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.04,
      "end_seconds": 56.99,
      "duration_seconds": 16.95,
      "text": "I get some relief from resting. It feels mild to me. And there's ankle swelling in the evenings as well, three weeks now. Poor sleep was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.03,
      "end_seconds": 75.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fainting, bruising or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.29,
      "end_seconds": 81.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "No fainting, bruising or coughing up blood, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.22,
      "end_seconds": 87.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any palpitations or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.15,
      "end_seconds": 92.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.71,
      "end_seconds": 96.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Alright, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.55,
      "end_seconds": 100.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.36,
      "end_seconds": 105.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.06,
      "end_seconds": 108.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.48,
      "end_seconds": 112.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.51,
      "end_seconds": 116.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Heart disease, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.28,
      "end_seconds": 129.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "Sure. Yes, heart disease is known to us, good to have that clear. What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.7,
      "end_seconds": 134.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.6,
      "end_seconds": 138.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.77,
      "end_seconds": 143.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.99,
      "end_seconds": 150.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.78,
      "end_seconds": 157.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Walnuts. I come out in... well, my lips swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.86,
      "end_seconds": 171.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.13,
      "end_seconds": 187.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.59,
      "end_seconds": 215.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.9,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 99 percent on room air, pulse 77, BP is 113 over 74, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.52,
      "end_seconds": 218.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.5,
      "end_seconds": 225.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "So, I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.12,
      "end_seconds": 231.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.77,
      "end_seconds": 235.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.41,
      "end_seconds": 256.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "The scar on your chest has healed well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.54,
      "end_seconds": 260.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.42,
      "end_seconds": 274.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Chest is clear and heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.08,
      "end_seconds": 279.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.6,
      "end_seconds": 305.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with stable recovery after the heart event."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.2,
      "end_seconds": 309.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.08,
      "end_seconds": 339.46,
      "duration_seconds": 28.38,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with stable recovery after the heart event do well once it's treated properly. A lipid profile is what I'd like next, for cardiovascular risk. I'm prescribing atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. It's for cardiovascular risk. Cardiac rehab is worth doing, it really helps your confidence. Let's get you seen by cardiac rehabilitation, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.22,
      "end_seconds": 351.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.08,
      "text": "If it hasn't settled in two weeks, we'd think about an ECG, but not now. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.19,
      "end_seconds": 356.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.39,
      "end_seconds": 358.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}